# Java / Bukkit patterns

## Main thread vs async
- Bukkit/Paper APIs that touch world, players, or scheduler must run on the **main thread**.
- DB I/O, heavy computation, or external calls must run **off** the main thread.

```java
// Async work (e.g. DB)
Bukkit.getScheduler().runTaskAsynchronously(plugin, () -> {
    // ... DB or heavy work ...
    // Then back to main if you need to touch server
    Bukkit.getScheduler().runTask(plugin, () -> {
        // ... update world/players ...
    });
});
```

- When async work finishes and you need to touch the server again, use `runTask(plugin, ...)` to hop back to main.

## Logging
- Use the project logger (e.g. `LWLogger` in `com.lula0802.LWEvents.logging`) where present, not `System.out` or raw `java.util.logging`.

## Config
- Prefer existing config helpers (e.g. `ConfigHelper`) and typed access; avoid ad-hoc `getConfig()` without going through project patterns.

## Naming
- Follow existing style in `SurvivalMain` and related classes (command/listener package layout under `com.lula0802.LWEvents`).
